# Build context for the production image.
#
# The Dockerfile's builder stage does `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is
# uploaded to the daemon and lands in a build layer. Before BEDO-004 that included the
# 28 MB reference video under docs/, the 39 MB of source assets, the whole test suite and
# every measurement artefact — none of which the build or the runtime touches.
#
# Keep this list aligned with what `npm run build` actually needs:
#   package*.json, index.html, src/, public/, tsconfig{,.app,.node}.json,
#   vite.config.ts, server.ts

# Installed and generated
node_modules
dist
test-results
playwright-report
measurements
*.tsbuildinfo

# Source assets the app does not load — see assets-source/README.md
assets-source

# Project evidence and documentation, including a 28 MB reference video
docs

# Tests and their configuration: never run inside the image
tests
vitest.config.ts
playwright.config.ts
tsconfig.test.json

# Tooling that runs on a developer machine or in CI, not in the image
scripts
# ...except the release scripts the build itself runs. `npm run build` generates the
# content-addressed runtime manifest (PERF-06) before Vite runs, so this one directory has
# to be in the build context or the image build fails with MODULE_NOT_FOUND.
!scripts/release
.oxlintrc.json
cloudbuild.yaml
push.sh
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md

# VCS, editors, OS noise
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
*.log
